# {project_name} Slices

Vertical slices are useful cuts through project behavior. Define slices by
intent first, then behavior contracts and implementation surfaces.

## Slices To Confirm

Use this shape for each slice. Keep `Status` as `Proposed` until the behavior
contract is approved. `Approved` authorizes implementation; `Landed` records
verified completion.

## Example Slice

- Status: Proposed
- Intent: <user or business outcome>
- Implementation surfaces: <repos or components>
- Depends on: <slice IDs or none>
- Domain terms: <terms from GLOSSARY.md>
- Data/privacy/security boundary: <boundary or none>
- Merge order: <surface order>

### BC-001 — <observable behavior>

- Given: <initial state>
- When: <action or event>
- Then: <observable outcome>
- Gate: <named test, contract check, QA step, runtime evidence, or smoke>
- Evidence: <test|contract|qa|runtime|smoke>: <durable locator> | <successful outcome; required when Landed>

Use 1-3 stable, unique `BC-*` IDs per approved slice. Never renumber or reuse an
ID. After landing, add `- Landed at: <repo@commit references>` and retain each
ID, its observable `Then`, `Gate`, and `Evidence` even if other detail is
groomed.
